comments.body:
This might be accepting just about any server error (I believe you intend for it to accept only "bad tx bytes" errors). And could therefore hide a real server bug.

I tried a mutant on it (in `ipc_fuzz.h`):

```diff
-    void consumeTransaction(CTransactionRef) {}
+    void consumeTransaction(CTransactionRef) { throw std::runtime_error("unexpected"); }
```

Which seemingly did not crash this fuzz target.

Among the many approaches we could take to make it more effective could be to first decode the bytes locally. Then the server may only fail when the local decode fails.

Such as:

<details>
<summary></summary>

```diff
+#include <streams.h>
+
 ...

     void sendTransactionPayload(std::vector<uint8_t> payload)
     {
+        bool expect_ok{true};
+        if (!payload.empty()) {
+            try {
+                SpanReader reader{payload};
+                ParamsStream stream{reader, TX_WITH_WITNESS};
+                CTransaction tx{deserialize, stream};
+            } catch (const std::ios_base::failure&) {
+                expect_ok = false;
+            }
+        }
+
 ...

