comments.body:
I tried this mutant (in `common-types.h`), specifically to see if raw UniValue branches checks if invalid JSON is rejected. It removes the rejection completely:

```diff
-        if (!value.read(std::string_view{data.begin(), data.size()})) {
-            throw std::runtime_error{"invalid JSON received over IPC"};
-        }
+        (void)value.read(std::string_view{data.begin(), data.size()});
```
The fuzz target did not catch it for the corpus I generated.

One possible option of killing it is the same approach as the tx one above. I tried it, and the response-side check catches the mutant (I didn't test the request side on its own).

